From 05b3333cb504c2f97b815d22acacf3633bb70c49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/36] ASoC: qdsp6: populate firmware-described TCL audio
 services

Q6ADM, Q6AFE and Q6ASM expose their child DAIs and clocks through OF
population. On the ACPI path those services exist under software nodes
and need explicit child construction and resource checks.

Populate recognized Q6AFE children and the opted-in Q6ASM DAI with
managed cleanup, parse DAI data through firmware properties, and require
usable translated DMA for the PCM consumer. Add clock platform matches,
validate non-OF clock attributes and publish explicit Q6AFE aliases.
Preserve the OF path and reject incomplete child descriptions. These
changes register DSP services and their clocks; a machine card and mixer
routes are still required for audible playback.
